course: dictionary
lesson: 7668
title: Proper: right, real and polite
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: "Proper" usually means right, correct or suitable for the situation. «Wear proper boots for the snow» means boots that suit the snow, not just any shoes. Ask yourself: is this the right way or the right thing for this job?
explain: "Proper" can also mean real or true. «She ate a proper meal, not just a snack.» A snack is small and quick; a proper meal is full and real. Here proper tells you the thing is the real thing, not a little bit of it.
explain: "Proper" can describe good behaviour too. «He has proper manners and always says thank you.» This means he follows the rules of good manners and is polite and well-behaved.
explain: In maths and grammar, proper has special names. A proper fraction, like 3/4, is less than one whole, because its top number is smaller than its bottom number. A proper noun is the name of one particular person, place or thing, like Sam or London, and it starts with a capital letter.
fact: Proper means right, correct or suitable for the situation.
fact: Proper can mean real or true, as in «a proper meal», not just a snack.
fact: Proper can mean polite and well-behaved, following the rules of good manners.
fact: A proper fraction is less than one whole, like 3/4, because its top number is smaller than its bottom number.
fact: A proper noun is the name of a particular person, place or thing, and it starts with a capital letter.
exercise: «Wear proper boots, because the path is muddy.» What does proper mean here? | *Suitable for the muddy weather | Very old and dusty | Pretty and sparkly | Too big for your feet
exercise: «She ate a proper meal, not just a snack.» What does proper suggest? | A cold meal left out | A meal eaten in the dark | A tiny, quick bite | *A real, full meal
exercise: London is a proper noun. Why does it start with a capital letter? | Because it is a fraction | Because it is the first word of every sentence | *It is the name of one particular place | Because all nouns start with a capital letter
test: Which of these is a proper fraction? | 7/7 | *3/4 | 5/3 | 9/2
test: «A proper sorry names what you did.» What does proper mean in this sentence? | Loud and dramatic | Quiet and sad | Too short to count | *Real and sincere, the right kind
exam: «Tom uses proper manners at the table.» What does proper mean here? | Very old | Loud and rude | Dirty and messy | *Polite and well-behaved
